+# Final review: cluster 10 (ports), epic hg-k4l
+
+Source: base 0dbe4772f4cd541e6b5ecaa1dd55b9a72f62c784, head efc21b65eb225578d3a623b29f23b3688849ea8b (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify`). Caller checkout observed at HEAD efc21b65, working tree clean; no changes to it were made or seen during the review.
+
+Cluster inputs: `src/ports/store.rs` (slice `slices/000066.diff`, +84 lines), with `digest.md` for context. The spec is `docs/superpowers/runs/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats/2026-11-05-seat-failure-manager-seats-design.md` at head (§4.2, the Key abstractions entry for StoreError, and the Requirement baseline).
+
+## What the cluster changes
+
+- It adds `StoreError::Integrity { holder, field, target, reason }`, which displays as `"{holder}: {field} {target} {reason}"`.
+- It adds the free function `unresolved(holder, field, target)`, the single constructor. Its default reason is "not found at the committed revision".
+- It adds `StoreError::because(reason)`. On an `Integrity` error it replaces only the reason. On every other variant it returns the error unchanged.
+- Two unit tests cover the constructor, the Display text, and the pass-through of `because` on a non-Integrity variant.
+
+## Spec conformance
+
+- §4.2 and Key abstractions ask for one store-level variant for "a reference does not resolve at the committed revision", built only by `unresolved(holder, field, target)`. The variant shape and the helper signature match the spec exactly.
+- The spec has wrong-kind and team-structure failures from `referenced_seat_template` map to the same variant. Cycles in `manager_chain` must surface the same way (§4.6). `because` serves those cases: `src/model/effective.rs:133,136` and `src/model/manager.rs:165` call it on `unresolved(..)` results. The digest records `because` as a deferred "extra-helper" minor. I agree that it is a modifier and not a second constructor, and it avoids duplicating the struct literal at each call site.
+- Single-constructor discipline: I ran `git grep` at head for `StoreError::Integrity` / `Integrity {`. Outside `src/ports/store.rs` it finds only pattern matches (bootstrap, cli::daemon_error, daemon::registry, plan::managers::reparent, writer, tests) and one field-by-field `Clone` impl in `src/store/instruction_source.rs:113`. No code outside the cluster builds the variant from scratch. There are 29 `unresolved(` call sites in `src/`.
+- Classification stays complete. `writer/mod.rs:95` maps `Integrity` together with `Corrupt` to `Fail::Data`. `daemon/registry.rs:70` maps `Integrity` to `CommandError::integrity` and every other variant to internal. No wildcard `StoreError` classifier was found that would quietly turn the new variant into a transient or I/O class.
+- The new variant introduces no IPC or record schema change (Global Constraints: no IPC_VERSION bump, no schema_version bump).
+
+## Requirement baseline trace
+
+- B4 (a named, non-transient integrity error for unresolved references, distinct from the transient case; the silent drops fail with it). This cluster delivers the store-level half: the named variant and its one constructor. The production path continues outside the cluster: `seat_reply` / `resolve_error` in `src/bootstrap/mod.rs` → `CommandError::from_store` in `src/daemon/registry.rs` → `IpcErrorCode::Integrity` → `cli::daemon_error` exit 6. That path belongs to the bootstrap, daemon and cli clusters and to the seam reviewer. It is not undelivered here.
+- No other baseline row is owned by this cluster. The manager-chain cycle and dangling-pointer errors (B5, B8, B9) reuse this variant through `unresolved(..).because(..)`. Their delivery is traced by the model/plan cluster reviewers.
+
+## Observations
+
+- The doc comment "Build only via `unresolved`" is a convention, not something the compiler enforces. Fields of a Rust enum variant are always public, so any module can write the literal. The grep above shows the convention holds at head. That is adequate for the spec, which only names a single helper.
+- Calling `because` on a non-Integrity error silently discards the requested reason. That is the documented behavior and is tested. Every current caller applies it directly to an `unresolved(..)` result, so no call site can lose its reason.
+- The Display text puts holder, field, target and reason in a fixed order. This makes some holders read awkwardly, such as bootstrap's `(seat, "record", seat)` triple ("st_x: record st_x not found ..."). That wording comes from call-site data in the bootstrap cluster, not from this cluster.
+- I did not run the tests in this review. Building requires the ht-build toolbox with a libz shim (see the task reports). Building in the caller worktree would also write to its `target/`. The task-1 report records the cluster's tests passing at its own head.
+
+## Findings
+
+- none
+
+## Verdict
+ready
+
+## Must fix before landing
+- none
+
+## Untested scope
+- No cluster test sets a multi-word holder or target containing ": " to check that the Display text stays parseable; all callers pass ids, so this is low risk.
+- The two unit tests in src/ports/store.rs were not re-run in this review (build environment needs the ht-build toolbox); evidence of a pass is the task-1 report only.
+
+## Deferred OK
+- StoreError::because goes beyond the brief's "unresolved is the only constructor helper" (task 1 deferred minor); it is a tested reason modifier used by effective.rs and manager.rs, not a second constructor.
+- "Build only via unresolved" on StoreError::Integrity is enforced by convention, not by the type system; grep at head shows no direct construction outside src/ports/store.rs apart from a field-wise Clone impl.
