+- finding-source · {"version":1,"source":"inv-17c351e9-bb55-40c3-8436-8b30e7f45319/cluster-17","artifact":"reviews/inv-17c351e9-bb55-40c3-8436-8b30e7f45319/final-review-inv-17c351e9-bb55-40c3-8436-8b30e7f45319.cluster-17.md","kind":"final-review","verdict":"ready","occurrences":[{"section":"Findings","position":1,"key":"tests/daemon_composed.rs `ORG_KINDS` lists `node_manager_set` but not `manager_edit`, apparently dropped when the hg-k4l.6 and hg-k4l.13 list edits merged. `every_kind_and_command_registered` therefore does not assert the ManagerEdit mutation. No coverage is lost, because `sweep_every_request_kind_has_a_mutation` in tests/integration_sweep.rs asserts it exhaustively.","text":"tests/daemon_composed.rs `ORG_KINDS` lists `node_manager_set` but not `manager_edit`, apparently dropped when the hg-k4l.6 and hg-k4l.13 list edits merged. `every_kind_and_command_registered` therefore does not assert the ManagerEdit mutation. No coverage is lost, because `sweep_every_request_kind_has_a_mutation` in tests/integration_sweep.rs asserts it exhaustively."},{"section":"Findings","position":2,"key":"The tests/seat_exit_codes.rs and tests/daemon_error_commands.rs fixtures bind a `UnixListener` at `root.herdr_socket()` and drain it on a thread. Every test then overrides `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH` to a nonexistent `dead.sock` or removes it, so the listener is never contacted. This is dead fixture code that suggests a \"reachable Herdr\" setup the tests do not actually use.","text":"The tests/seat_exit_codes.rs and tests/daemon_error_commands.rs fixtures bind a `UnixListener` at `root.herdr_socket()` and drain it on a thread. Every test then overrides `HERDR_SOCKET_PATH` to a nonexistent `dead.sock` or removes it, so the listener is never contacted. This is dead fixture code that suggests a \"reachable Herdr\" setup the tests do not actually use."},{"section":"Findings","position":3,"key":"tests/daemon_free_reads.rs `assert!(!f.sock_exists())` is a weak guard that these reads use NoEnsure. An Ensure-mode read would also leave no socket here, because the spawned daemon cannot reach the unbound Herdr socket. The exit-5 assertion, which is the requirement, is unaffected.","text":"tests/daemon_free_reads.rs `assert!(!f.sock_exists())` is a weak guard that these reads use NoEnsure. An Ensure-mode read would also leave no socket here, because the spawned daemon cannot reach the unbound Herdr socket. The exit-5 assertion, which is the requirement, is unaffected."},{"section":"Findings","position":4,"key":"tests/node_manager_warning.rs `assert!(stdout(&before).contains(\"s\"))` is near-vacuous. It was already recorded as a task-14 deferred minor. The later `assert_eq!(stdout(&after), stdout(&before))` carries the real stdout-stability check.","text":"tests/node_manager_warning.rs `assert!(stdout(&before).contains(\"s\"))` is near-vacuous. It was already recorded as a task-14 deferred minor. The later `assert_eq!(stdout(&after), stdout(&before))` carries the real stdout-stability check."},{"section":"Concerns","position":1,"key":"The new integration tests were not re-run by this review at efc21b6. Their pass status at the integrated head depends on the epic's final full-suite run.","text":"The new integration tests were not re-run by this review at efc21b6. Their pass status at the integrated head depends on the epic's final full-suite run."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":1,"key":"Exit 6 (graph integrity) has no spawned-binary test for `seat` or for any other command; it is covered only by `classify`/`seat_failure` unit tests in src/cli (spec §4.4 row \"graph integrity\").","text":"Exit 6 (graph integrity) has no spawned-binary test for `seat` or for any other command; it is covered only by `classify`/`seat_failure` unit tests in src/cli (spec §4.4 row \"graph integrity\")."},{"section":"Untested scope","position":2,"key":"No spawned-binary test covers a hung daemon (read timeout to Frame) or a still-starting daemon (`Remote{Unavailable}`